{"text":"Whole-outcome correction replacing unclaimed 894c9030 for audit55563589/reviewf24d2b56. Builder: one duty ledger, an alarm step table, git migrations, and the Room out of git's tables (simplification review 55563589, findings ARCH-01, ARCH-06, ARCH-08, LAYER-01). (1) The remote-step duty ledger exists three times: git/src/workspace/workspaces.ts:218-307, git/src/snapshot/repos.ts:245-277 and hand copies in room/src/jobs.ts:73-84, 216-219 (historical duplication; completeInventory/refusedUnchanged already exported and jobs already imports completeInventory at a6330262), with the backoff formula at seven sites with differing caps and the keyed lock at three. Add DutyLedger, backoff and KeyedLock in git, export refusedUnchanged, completeInventory and redact, delete the copies. (2) The Room writes git's private artroom_ws_duty (core.ts:1368) and reads artroom_ws (core.ts:1708); credit D5 retirement of the legacy-import path and add an owning Workspaces.hasPendingProvision predicate for the remaining direct read and forbid artroom_ table names in room/src with a grep test. (3) core.ts:1628-1643 lists alarm steps while nextAlarm (:1672-1715) separately knows each step's tables; make steps a record of run and due with nextAlarm as the minimum. (4) git's ten tables are created in constructors with no version (workspaces.ts:164-177; landing/core.ts:103-107; snapshot/repos.ts:135-152 already has transactional version2 adoption/upgrade at the original baseline) while the Room has a migration runner (store.ts:97-109); move the runner to git/src/sql.ts, give each git component versioned migrations that adopt existing unversioned tables idempotently, and route the stray writes to previews, ws_leases and meta through their owning module. Current reconciliation: Credit existing snapshot transactional schema/adoption at93/a633 and later73eccbec D5 retirement; do not repeat a completed upgrade or revive the retired importLegacyDuties path. Credit exported inventory helpers/current imports. Keep one shared ledger/backoff/keyed lock and full run/due table/owner APIs for surviving private-table and previews/ws_leases/meta writes. Current core.ts:2000 still reads artroom_ws. Preserve current tables/state/unknown effects and referenced closed ownership. Any migration adoption test uses still-supported historical state and retains compatible readers; no unknown remote effect can disappear. Historical findings/counts/lines below are dated at93a2552e/a6330262, not fresh current-main assertions. Reconcile with reviewed main 344656705140d9bf6539fe44de889d1e21dd2482 and credit already delivered work. All original functional groups remain owed except explicitly credited prior implementations. Schedule acts enabling jam first, then spikes needed for concrete jam work, then jam and the full67-page Artroom docs in parallel (user7363396b/04da4388). No blanket before-J2/J3/public-deployment or empty-backlog readiness gate is added; no deployment is commissioned.","body":{"conditions":"One ledger implementation with the existing tables and states unchanged; room/src contains no artroom_ table name; steps and nextAlarm derive from one table with a test that a new step cannot be stranded; git migrations versioned with an adoption test over a pre-existing unversioned database; root gates pass; checker review.","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8592926f1d4d30e3cf282eadc411dacde51d3ac0 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7a3bbf8f3b7ccc7ba4fd596a6bcfe5756d51a77e","target_head":"344656705140d9bf6539fe44de889d1e21dd2482","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"},"expectation":{"request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:894c903023fbc4fb66bb26aba93068d76338308a","retirement":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#gi